From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ninjacornix <milanvrankic@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:30:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(editor): join the script doc loader thread only from the
 main thread

Meant for upstream: a general race fix in EditorHelp.

_finish_regen_script_doc_thread() ran on worker_thread and joined
loader_thread, the thread that had just started it. The main thread
joins loader_thread too, in regenerate_script_doc_cache(), and
Thread::start() publishes the thread id before it stores the
std::thread. When the worker's join lost either race, std::thread::join
threw, and the editor ended in std::terminate (0xC0000409 on Windows).
It showed on a slow software-rendered Windows runner, about one first
editor launch of a fresh project in ten.

Now only the main thread joins loader_thread: before restarting it,
waiting for it ahead of worker_thread (which it starts as its last
step), and in cleanup_doc().
---
 editor/doc/editor_help.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/editor/doc/editor_help.cpp b/editor/doc/editor_help.cpp
index a469a50..f7b9716 100644
--- a/editor/doc/editor_help.cpp
+++ b/editor/doc/editor_help.cpp
@@ -3173,14 +3173,17 @@ void EditorHelp::regenerate_script_doc_cache() {
 		return;
 	}
 
-	_wait_for_thread(worker_thread);
+	// The loader thread starts the worker thread as its last step, so wait for it first.
 	_wait_for_thread(loader_thread);
+	_wait_for_thread(worker_thread);
 	loader_thread.start(_regen_script_doc_thread, EditorFileSystem::get_singleton()->get_filesystem());
 }
 
 // Runs on worker_thread since it writes to DocData.
+// The loader thread is only ever joined from the main thread: joining it here as well
+// raced with the main thread, both with its own join and with Thread::start() still
+// storing the new thread, and the failed join ended the editor in std::terminate.
 void EditorHelp::_finish_regen_script_doc_thread(void *p_udata) {
-	loader_thread.wait_to_finish();
 	_process_postponed_docs();
 	_script_docs_loaded.set();
 
@@ -3363,6 +3366,7 @@ void EditorHelp::update_doc() {
 }
 
 void EditorHelp::cleanup_doc() {
+	_wait_for_thread(loader_thread);
 	_wait_for_thread();
 	memdelete(doc);
 	doc = nullptr;
